// Plugin: no-manual-token-estimate — a hand-rolled `<expr>.length / 4` token estimate.
//
// Catches:    Any `$x.length / 4` — the classic "≈ 4 chars per token" hand-roll — in
//             packages/{client,ui,server}/src. `@orb/kit/tokens` is the ONE token
//             estimator: `estimateTokens(text)` (the OpenRouter "QuadChars" algorithm —
//             printable-ASCII/4 PLUS one-per-non-ASCII-codepoint, so it does NOT
//             undercount CJK/emoji ~4× the way a flat `length/4` does; a CJK transcript
//             silently overflows a `length/4` budget — see chat/memory .../token-guard.ts).
//
//               ❌ const tokens = text.length / 4;
//               ✅ import { estimateTokens } from "@orb/kit/tokens";
//                  const tokens = estimateTokens(text);
//
// Scope:      packages/{client,ui,server}/src (server assembles prompts too — the estimate
//             is used across assembly/history-budget/memory/pipeline/card-tokens/buddy).
//             The estimator's own home is packages/kit/src/tokens/ — outside this scope,
//             so kit is not reached. Skips tests/tooling.
//
// Low-FP by design: `<member>.length / 4` has near-zero non-token meaning. If a genuine
//             non-token divide-by-4-of-a-length ever appears, suppress WITH a reason.
//
// Refs:       packages/kit/src/tokens/index.ts (estimateTokens — the ONE estimator)
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// GritQL note: a snippet pattern parses to AST, so `$x.length / 4` matches regardless of
// whitespace (`x.length/4` too) and binds `$x` to any object expression (`foo.bar.length`
// included). It matches the binary-expression node anywhere — inside `Math.ceil(...)`,
// a return, an assignment.

language js

`$x.length / 4` as $node where {
  $filename <: r".*/packages/(?:client|ui|server)/src/.*",
  $filename <: not or {
    r".*\.test\.tsx?$",
    r".*/tests/.*"
  },
  register_diagnostic(span=$node, message="hand-rolled `.length / 4` token estimate — @orb/kit/tokens is the ONE estimator: import { estimateTokens } and call estimateTokens(text). A flat length/4 undercounts CJK/emoji ~4× and silently overflows token budgets. See packages/kit/src/tokens/index.ts.")
}
